# `cig run` on each engine, 2026-11-25: the tree-walker, the VM, the default, and the default against other languages

<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0 -->

The {{programs.cig-tree}} programs of [`bench/compute`](../bench/compute/), run by one build of cig four ways: `cig run --engine tree`; `cig run --engine vm` with the script's module already in the tin; `cig run --engine vm` with nothing in the tin, so every run lowers the script before it runs it; and `cig run` on the default (cig-script#259's `auto`: the VM when a module is kept for the script, else the tree-walker, with a `cig __lower` left behind after a script's second run to lower it and keep the module). In the same rounds the same programs were run in Lua, LuaJIT, CPython, Node and Rust, so `cig run` as it now is by default stands beside them. It was measured for [#254](https://github.com/otmof-ops/cig-script/issues/254) and [#259](https://github.com/otmof-ops/cig-script/issues/259), which made `auto` the default `cig run` takes.

The machine is a development machine (the conditions are below), not the benchmark paper's test machine: read the ratios; the times belong to this machine. cig is built from commit `7e76bb8` (merged to `main` as `cebd9dd`, [#287](https://github.com/otmof-ops/cig-script/pull/287)) as its release workflow builds it for Linux (`cargo build --release --target x86_64-unknown-linux-musl`): no release has `auto` yet, and the build still reports itself as `cig 1.25.0`, the last release's version. [The 1.25.0 release's run](ENGINES-1.25.0.md) measured the two engines, three ways, before `auto` existed.

Every measured number here is made from the samples in [`bench/results/2026-11-25-engines/main/`](../bench/results/2026-11-25-engines/main/) by [`bench/compare/report.py`](../bench/compare/report.py), and made again by [`bench/compare/check.py`](../bench/compare/check.py), a second program written apart from the first to [the same definitions](../bench/compare/SPEC.md).

## In short

- **With its module in the tin, the VM runs the {{n.compute.cig-vm.cig-tree}} compute programs in {{geomean.compute.cig-vm.cig-tree}} of the tree-walker's time**, {{inverse.compute.cig-vm.cig-tree}} times as fast: faster on {{faster.compute.cig-vm.cig-tree}}, level on {{level.compute.cig-vm.cig-tree}}, slower on {{slower.compute.cig-vm.cig-tree}}. It gains the most on `{{lowest.compute.cig-vm.cig-tree}}` and the least on `{{highest.compute.cig-vm.cig-tree}}`.
- **`cig run` on the default is on the VM** from a script's third run on: the measurement here is `cig-auto` beside `cig-vm`. Over the {{n.compute.cig-auto.cig-vm}} compute programs the default takes {{geomean.compute.cig-auto.cig-vm}} of asking for the VM directly, and {{geomean.compute.cig-auto.cig-tree}} of the tree-walker's: {{faster.compute.cig-auto.cig-tree}} of {{n.compute.cig-auto.cig-tree}} programs are faster than the tree-walker on the default, level on {{level.compute.cig-auto.cig-tree}} and slower on {{slower.compute.cig-auto.cig-tree}}.
- **A first run of the VM pays for the lowering.** With nothing in the tin a run on `--engine vm` lowers the script, verifies and loads the module, and keeps it. On the compute programs that comes to {{geomean.compute.cig-vm-cold.cig-tree}} of the tree-walker's time, faster on {{faster.compute.cig-vm-cold.cig-tree}} of {{n.compute.cig-vm-cold.cig-tree}}. On the default no run does the lowering itself: a script's first two runs are the tree-walker's, and the second leaves the lowering to a process of its own. [A script's first runs](ENGINES-FIRST-RUNS-2026-11-25.md) measures them.
- **Against other languages, on the default:** `cig run` takes {{geomean.compute.cig.lua}} times Lua 5.4's time at the geometric mean of the {{n.compute.cig.lua}} compute programs both have, {{geomean.compute.cig.luajit-off}} times that of LuaJIT's interpreter, {{geomean.compute.cig.luajit}} times LuaJIT's, {{geomean.compute.cig.python}} times CPython 3.12's and {{geomean.compute.cig.node}} times Node 18's. Under 1, cig took less time. [The table is below](#against-other-languages).

